```ADD_PAPER
2508.01682v1
This paper presents BiPRM, a novel bidirectional evaluation framework for process reward modeling that overcomes the limitations of conventional left-to-right approaches. By introducing a parallel right-to-left evaluation stream, BiPRM allows later reasoning steps to retrospectively validate and refine earlier ones, leading to significantly improved accuracy in assessing intermediate reasoning quality—demonstrated by up to a 31.9% improvement over traditional methods. The extensive experiments detailed in the study underscore how bidirectional reasoning, when integrated with tailored prompt engineering techniques, enhances the capture of nuanced quality signals. These findings are particularly relevant for designing two-stage, bi-directional systems for peer review where both author feedback and reviewer rewards are dynamically adjusted, ensuring robust and precise measurement of review quality in AI conferences.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
