```ADD_PAPER
2507.18618v1
This paper introduces TRPrompt, a unified framework for prompt optimization that leverages fine-grained, textual rewards to iteratively calibrate prompt performance for large language models. By bootstrapping query-aware prompt adjustments based on both numerical and descriptive feedback, the approach demonstrates substantial improvements in reasoning tasks, notably on challenging mathematical benchmarks. The experimental results illustrate that dynamic, reward-guided prompt tuning significantly boosts evaluation accuracy by effectively capturing subtle quality and contextual signals. The techniques proposed in TRPrompt are highly relevant to our goal of designing a two-stage, bi-directional peer-review system: they provide a blueprint for integrating adaptive prompt engineering with dynamic reward signals to refine both author feedback and reviewer evaluations. This bidirectional, iterative adjustment mechanism is critical for capturing nuanced quality metrics in peer review, ensuring that both constructive criticism and positive reinforcement are accurately measured and leveraged.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
