^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ literature review ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
```ADD_PAPER
2509.21880v1
In "No Prompt Left Behind: Exploiting Zero-Variance Prompts in LLM Reinforcement Learning via Entropy-Guided Advantage Shaping," the authors tackle the often-overlooked challenge of zero-variance prompts—situations where all model responses yield identical rewards and, hence, provide little teaching signal. To turn these seemingly uninformative prompts into a valuable source of error sensitivity, the paper introduces a novel algorithm that leverages token-level feedback modulated by entropy-guided advantage shaping. Extensive experiments on six mathematics reasoning benchmarks demonstrate that the method significantly refines policy optimization by rewarding correctness and penalizing subtle errors even when contrasting signals are absent. This approach yields notable accuracy gains over standard reward modeling techniques and offers a compelling strategy for enhancing reward signal granularity. The experimental findings suggest that the techniques described could be effectively adapted to a two-stage, bidirectional peer-review framework, where dynamic, token-informed adjustments to both author feedback and reviewer rewards can lead to a more nuanced and precise evaluation of review quality in AI conferences.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
